@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title GitHub SSH host keys — git@github.com in an sbx world
' purpose: why git pull origin fails in proveo run cursor, and the host-key write that closes it
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: defs/base/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/base/ssh/github_known_hosts
' covers: defs/cursor/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/cecli/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/codex/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh
' covers: internal/contract/github_ssh_hosts_test.go
'   launch env (t=0) .............. _spec/internal/sbx/launch-env.puml
'   HTTPS credential injection .... _spec/cmd/proveo/github-credentials.puml
'   seed step order ............... _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.

node "proveo/base image" as IMG <<host>> {
  database """/etc/ssh/ssh_known_hosts""\nbaked GitHub host keys" as SYS <<db>>
}

node "Agent at t≈0" as AG <<host>> {
  component "ssh + forwarded agent" as SSH <<app>>
  component "git pull origin" as PULL <<app>>
}

node "Startup (late / old images)" as SEED <<app>> {
  component """proveo_seed""\nseed_github_known_hosts" as SEEDFN <<app>>
  database "~/.ssh/known_hosts" as KH <<db>>
}

cloud "api.github.com/meta\nssh_keys over HTTPS" as META <<cloud>>
component "empty known_hosts\nHost key verification failed" as FAIL <<error>>

IMG ARROW_MAIN SYS
SYS ARROW_MAIN SSH : t=0, no TTY needed
SSH ARROW_MAIN PULL : origin stays git@github.com
SEEDFN ARROW_CLOUD META
META ARROW_OPTIONAL KH : images that predate the bake
KH ARROW_OPTIONAL SSH
FAIL ARROW_ERROR PULL : errorLabel(before the bake)

note bottom of FAIL
  **The abort this file closes.** origin is
  copied as git@github.com, SSH reaches
  GitHub, and the host agent is forwarded,
  but known_hosts is empty and there is no
  TTY, so git pull dies on host-key check.
end note

note right of SYS
  **Bake the keys, keep the transport.**
  OpenSSH already looks in
  /etc/ssh/ssh_known_hosts. That file is
  in the image so a mixin agent can git
  pull before kit startup finishes.
end note

note right of KH
  **Seed is the old-image path.**
  proveo_seed fetches ssh_keys from
  api.github.com/meta over HTTPS when the
  image has no GitHub keys, the same
  source Docker's github-ssh kit uses.
end note

note bottom of META
  **Never ssh-keyscan.** The meta endpoint
  is HTTPS, so it works through the proxy
  when port 22 is policy-blocked, and it
  tracks GitHub's rotations for images
  that have not been rebuilt yet.
end note
@enduml
